📦 Inventory Management System (React.js)

A simple and efficient Inventory Management System built using React.js, designed to help users add, edit, delete, and track products with an intuitive UI.
This project is part of my React.JS Projects Practice collection.

🚀 Features
✅ Core Functionalities

Add New Items – Add products with attributes like name, quantity, category, price, etc.

Edit Existing Items – Update details instantly with form-based editing.

Delete Items – Remove unwanted or outdated inventory.

Real-time Updates – React state updates for smooth UI interactions.

Search / Filter (optional depending on your code) – Quickly find products.

🎨 UI/UX

Clean, simple, beginner-friendly interface

Responsive layout

Fast interactions using React hooks

🛠️ Tech Stack
Technology	Purpose
React.js	Frontend UI framework

CSS / Tailwind / Styled Components 	Styling
Local Storage 

📦 Installation & Setup

Follow these steps to run the project locally:

1️⃣ Clone the Repository
git clone https://github.com/YUMESHBAN/React.JS-Projects-Practice.git

2️⃣ Navigate Into the Inventory Management Project

(Replace folder-name with the actual folder name if different)

cd inventory-management

3️⃣ Install Dependencies
npm install

4️⃣ Start the Development Server
npm start


The app will run on:
👉 http://localhost:3000/

🧪 Usage Guide

Open the app in your browser

Use the form to add new inventory items

Click Edit to modify any item

Click Delete to remove items

View list updates instantly on screen

📈 Future Improvements (Optional Add-Ons)

Connect with backend API (Node/Express + MongoDB)

Add authentication for secure access

Implement pagination for large inventories

Add export to CSV / Excel functionality

Add charts / analytics dashboard

